@startuml
title SSD 4 — Join and Manage Waiting List (iteration 2)
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
actor "Patient / AdministrativeStaff" as Requester
actor AdministrativeStaff as Staff
participant ":System" as System
Requester -> System: searchAvailability(serviceID, professionalID?, locationID?, dateRange, specialtyID?)
System --> Requester: [] — No availability
Requester -> System: joinWaitingList(patientID, serviceID, locationID,\nprofessionalID?, specialtyID?, dateRange?, referralID?)
alt valid patient, criteria, and no matching available slots
  System --> Requester: entryID, status = waiting, priorityRank
else invalid criteria, patient missing, or matching availability now exists
  System --> Requester: invalidInput / notFound / availabilityExists / accessDenied
end
opt staff adjusts priority
  Staff -> System: changeWaitingListPriority(entryID, priorityRank)
  System --> Staff: entryID, priorityRank (or validation failure)
end
opt staff removes an entry
  Staff -> System: removeWaitingListEntry(entryID)
  System --> Staff: entryID, status = removed (or validation failure)
end
note over Requester,System
Patient can join only for self. Staff alone changes priority/removes entries.
At least one preference (professional, specialty, or date range) must be supplied.
searchAvailability uses the same optional filters as SSDs 1 and 3;
all supplied filters must match.
Staff controls priority; no additional tie-breaking policy is specified.
end note
@enduml
